ITEMS=[
("Several recent, verified closings of very similar homes exist in an owner-occupied subdivision. Its rental evidence is weak, and estimating depreciation on older homes is difficult. Which reconciliation choice is best supported?",
 ["Give the most weight to the sales comparison approach","Give the most weight to the cost approach","Give the most weight to the income approach","Weight the three approaches equally"],
 "The sales comparison indication has the strongest direct market evidence in this assignment; weighting should follow evidence quality, not a fixed equal split."),
("A newly completed specialized residence has reliable land sales and detailed current construction costs with negligible depreciation. Available improved sales are dissimilar and rental data are sparse. Which indication deserves greatest initial weight on these facts?",
 ["Give the most weight to the cost approach","Give the most weight to the sales comparison approach","Give the most weight to the income approach","Average the approaches without weighting"],
 "Reliable land and current cost evidence with little depreciation can make the cost indication most persuasive in this stated setting."),
("Buyers of a small rental property consistently price comparable properties from verified net income and supported capitalization rates. Construction costs are dated and comparable sale details are incomplete. Which indication has the strongest stated support?",
 ["Give the most weight to the income approach","Give the most weight to the sales comparison approach","Give the most weight to the cost approach","Use the lowest indication as a conservative value"],
 "The income indication best reflects the identified purchasers and the strongest available evidence. Choosing the lowest figure is not reconciliation."),
("Two otherwise well-supported approaches differ sharply. Inspection of the worksheets shows one uses 1,800 square feet and the other uses 2,400 square feet for the same building. What should the appraiser do before assigning weights?",
 ["Correct the building size data first","Average the two indications","Give more weight to the higher indication","Give more weight to the lower indication"],
 "A factual inconsistency must be investigated and corrected before reconciliation; weighting cannot repair incompatible input data."),
]
